WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.890
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:07.069
The humble caterpillar is one of the most
mind-shatteringly incredulous creatures on

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:08.069
planet Earth.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:11.190
There’s so much more to this chubby worm
than meets the eye.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:16.340
If there was a prize for the animal most likely
to be a Pokemon, then this suave fella would

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.140
take gold, because it evolves not once but
twice.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.560
First from a larva to a caterpillar then finally
into a beautiful butterfly.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.840
Actually, it’s so alike a Pokemon it already
is one.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:37.460
But how does a living, organic thing metamorphosise
so consistently and so perfectly into a completely

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.600
different creature, of an entirely different
shape and size?

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.219
You may be either grossed out when I tell
you this, or totally amazed… but inside

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:57.109
the chrysalis the caterpillar completely liquidises,
turning into a mush of gooey proteins and

00:00:57.109 --> 00:01:01.050
fibres, as it slowly reforms into a butterfly
over 10 days.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.710
We’ll talk about metamorphosis more later
but first, let’s start from the beginning

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.520
of this incredible insect’s life-cycle.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.390
Because this amazing insect has so many secrets
up its sleeve, or wings, that you’re not

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.550
going to want to miss any of it.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:22.090
A female butterfly will find a nice looking
tree and lay its tiny eggs on the underside

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:27.490
of the tree’s leaves, each egg contains
a tiny, tiny caterpillar lava.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:33.770
But the mother is extremely picky about which
plant gets to play host to her eggs, each

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:37.345
different species of butterfly uses a different
species of plant and only that species of

00:01:37.345 --> 00:01:41.910
plant to lay its eggs upon.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:47.120
This is all made a thousand times more complicated
when you consider that there are over 20,000

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.910
species of butterfly in the world.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:56.140
The egg is the size of a pinhead and the mother
will lay 500 eggs at a time.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:01.320
It then takes just four days for the egg to
hatch, by this point the lava is freaking

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:06.590
starving so it eats its way out of its own
egg then eats the rest of the eggshell, as

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:13.080
well as the entire leaf its on and it will
probably have a good go at the leaf next to

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.080
it aswell.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:20.200
This first meal is dangerous because the various
sticky residues found inside some species

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:25.230
of leaves can cause the caterpillar lava’s
mouth to gum up.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.689
Many caterpillars die from this.

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:33.540
If it survives the great feast, then all this
sustenance gives the greedy little fella energy

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.659
to grow into several times its size.

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:41.099
It will then take a break to shed its first
layer of skin.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:45.810
The caterpillar will then spend the next week
eating leaves and growing into a full-sized

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.810
caterpillar.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:51.129
Once fully-grown this ravenous tyrant can
eat a full leaf in under an hour.

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:56.249
Once the caterpillar has gotten all nice and
fat it prepares for the big change.

00:02:56.249 --> 00:03:02.269
It finds a nice quiet spot underneath a branch
and spins itself a silk button to attach itself

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:04.280
to the underside of the branch.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.920
Other species get even fancier and spin a
fine silk harness that they then sit inside.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.780
Now begins the magic trick – it’s commonly
thought that the caterpillar now makes its

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:22.060
chrysalis, also known as a pupa, but not a
cocoon, that’s something else.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.889
But it in fact grows this hardened shell underneath
its top layer of skin in the week leading

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:30.779
up to its metamorphosis.

00:03:30.779 --> 00:03:36.169
So when the time comes, all it has to do is
shed its top layer of skin and its protective

00:03:36.169 --> 00:03:40.680
pupa is all ready, for the transformation
to begin.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.969
But the caterpillar has another magic trick
up its sleeve.

00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:51.680
To disguise itself from predators, the pupa
will change its colour to exactly match that

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.739
of whatever is behind it.

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:59.669
And so the transformation begins, taking roughly
two weeks to turn from a furry slug into a

00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:02.389
beautiful, winged insect.

00:04:02.389 --> 00:04:07.730
But if you were able to see inside the pupa
whilst this is taking place, you might be

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.280
rather horrified.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:15.109
The transformation begins with the caterpillar
releasing digestive enzymes to eat itself

00:04:15.109 --> 00:04:19.799
alive; effectively turning itself into a soup.

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:20.799
Yuck.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:27.810
If you were to cut open a pupa at the right
time during metamorphosis, a goo would ooze

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.810
out.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:35.740
But this magic goo contains everything needed
to create a butterfly, and that is rather

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:36.780
incredible.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.220
But not every cell liquefies.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:45.781
Certain groups of highly organized cells remain
as solids within the soup.

00:04:45.781 --> 00:04:50.729
Over the course of two weeks this caterpillar
curry slowly turns into a butterfly broth

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:55.310
and then into an actual butterfly, all from
a gooey liquid.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:05:01.220
It’s such an incredible phenomenon that
scientists still aren’t quite sure how this

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.110
liquid organizes itself into a butterfly.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:09.150
What’s so amazing about all of this is that
everything about the creature changes during

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:14.439
the transformation, its shape, its taste,
how it eats, how it moves and how it senses

00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:21.060
– yet the butterfly is still able to remember
its life as a caterpillar.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:25.190
You would think that your brain being turned
into a soup then reshaped into an entirely

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:28.020
new brain would erase all of your memories.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:33.330
But a recent study showed that butterflies
were able to remember the solution to a puzzle

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.669
that they were taught how to solve, when they
were a caterpillar.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:43.699
Meaning some of the synaptic connections in
the caterpillar’s brain survive the soupification.

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:53.289
Making the humble caterpillar one of the true
wonders of 

00:05:53.289 --> 00:05:57.710
the natural world.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:04.100
Thanks for watching.

